Z||000004||fastback87||10-30-2001||12:10 AM||||I had the same problem and it is easy to diagnose and fix if it is the same problem I had.<P>1.  Pull the fuel pump fuse it is like the second one from the left, closest to you if you are sitting in the seat. "I think"<P>2.  With the ignition off pull that fuse and see if the sound stops.  If so the it is definitely the pump, and go to step 3.  If not don't even bother reading on cause it wont help you. ;-)<P>3.  Put the fuse back in and you should hear the pump run again.  Then unplug your oil pressure sending unit electrical plug, if the sound stops then you have a bad oil pressure sensor and need to replace that...problem solved.  If not...<P>4.  Unplug the fuel pump relay and check it.  It is behind the air cleaner on a V6 or in the engine compartment right behind the drivers head rest.  If the noise stops when you unplug it then it could be the relay or burnt wires going to the relay.  Trace the wiring and see if it is melted or shorted.<P>***Just as another check to see if it is the fuel pump take the negative battery cable off, get a mulitester, set it up to read amps, touch it to the cable and the battery to complete the connection (BE SURE the key is OFF, your tester is 10A or more and fuse protected).  If it is your fuel pump, and all the lights are off except the trunk light which pulls 1A each your reading for the fuel pump is between 3 and 4 amps.<P>I noticed the problem when I stopped driving my car everyday and more like 1-2 times a week.  I was having to jumpstart my car all the time.  4A can kill a battery (to the point of not starting the car) in about 48 -72 hours.  My oil pressure read fine but the problem was the sending unit.  It has two sensors a pressure switch that turns on at 4 PSI and a sensor that monitors oil pressure.  My problem was the switch part, the switch is set up so when the ECM reads that there is pressure at the switch it automatically starts the fuel pump until the pressure is less than 4 PSI.  This took me about a month to figure out and costs about $30 at AutoZone and it was on the shelf.  I hope this helps.<P>Does anyone have an extra A/C bracket for a V6?||||reg||12
